cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the article given under
  preferred-citation. The supplementary data are archived at Zenodo
  (see identifiers).
type: software
title: "etlscan: acquisition and analysis software for depth-resolved imaging with electronically tunable lenses"
abstract: >-
  Acquisition and analysis software for imaging systems built around an
  electronically tunable lens (ETL). The acquisition steps the focal plane
  through a water column, one plane per camera frame. The analysis tracks
  multiple individuals, recovers their depth from focus peaks
  (depth-from-focus), reconstructs three-dimensional trajectories and
  measures in-focus specimens. A realtime mode stores sharp crops during
  acquisition.
